{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv57iMsSqqjBNNb1ZaXN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 006 is done, and it clears the whole WI-887 change set. All of sitting 005's findings were fixed in commit `4c9a4271b`, so this time nothing goes back.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=10`.** I'd bless all ten amended rows (LLR-045, LLR-140, LLR-207, LLR-262, LLR-269, LLR-270, LLR-305, TC-205, TC-266, TC-322). Each one changes what is required, but the new text holds together and traces to an approved parent.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=2`, for SR-239 and TC-351.**\n- **SR-239:** the rule that a malformed setting reads as off now has its own \"If … then\" clause, so it can actually apply. Gate admission is left to SR-156 instead of being restated. The link back to its need SN-025 is added and the decision-id citation is gone.\n- **TC-351:** all 21 tests it names exist, and the parent it checks is now approved.\n\n**Commits**, all ending with `WI: WI-887`:\n\n| Commit | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `3fbff4f4d` | The verdict file, `docs/reviews/wi-887/006-ADJUDICATE-4c9a427.md` |\n| `2b3dfd33c` | Re-attestation of the ten amended rows (act seq 108, citing the verdict) |\n| `54f2f5dd0` | SR-239 and TC-351 flipped to `Approved`, with the snapshot of both registries (act seq 109) |\n\nThe two status lines were the only registry cells I changed.\n\nThe re-attestation act ran before the approval act, although the verdict judges SR-239 first. The approval act's copy of `test-cases.toml` would have been refused while TC-205, TC-266 and TC-322 were still drifted. All three acts sit in the same sitting under the same verdict.\n\n`trace.py --strict-integrity` passes, and `trace.py --strict` raises no advisory on SR-239, TC-351, LLR-305 or TC-322.\n\nTwo things are still open for the lane: decision D-001 is still waiting on your review, and the `.requested` binding file is untracked, left for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":426236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":716},"output_tokens":743,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d52360a6-7377-4d1e-a658-4cbc4052baa8","uuid":"9e3bfa7f-0236-4997-9bd4-78d26d9020f5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:41:00.484Z","request_id":"req_011Cfv57hjfcrNWt5CZymbCE"}
